[Music]  as commissioner for health and food  safety  one of my top political priorities is  animal welfare  a file that is as much a priority for  this commission as it is close to my  heart  your voice was heard loud and clear  through the european citizens initiative  and the cage age  you showed us that you want to have your  say and that you want europe to change  course on this issue and i can tell you  that europe will change course on animal  welfare  last june we gave our pledge that we  will by the end of 2023 put forward  legislation to start phasing out the use  of cages for certain farm animals  but we will go further than that  and  as announced in the farm-to-folk  strategy  also in 2023 we will revise all eu rules  on animal welfare our ambition is clear  we want to strengthen and expand the  protections afforded to animals in many  key areas  that includes better living and  transport conditions and enhanced  protection of animals during slaughter  europe needs ambition and conviction to  act on an issue which is so important to  european citizens  to do this  we need your input  and your views  on how to share the proposal  and this is why i turn to you once again  to help us build a better future for  animals in the eu  by letting us know what your concerns  and aspirations are on this important  issue  europe is already a place that respects  nurtures  and upholds the welfare of billions of  animals  whether they roam our countryside graze  our farmlands or form an integral part  of our families as pets  but we need to do more  we want to do more  and we are determined to do more  because animal welfare matters  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  you

